sequenceDiagram
    participant App as Request thread
    participant L as Logger
    participant C as ConsoleAppender
    participant A as AsyncAppender
    participant W as Worker thread
    participant F as FileAppender

    App->>L: info order accepted
    Note over L: level is at or above the threshold, so continue
    Note over L: timestamp, thread name and trace id are captured here on the request thread
    L->>C: append event
    C-->>L: printed
    L->>A: append event
    A->>A: enqueue, blocks only if the queue is full
    A-->>L: returns immediately
    L-->>App: returns

    W->>A: take next event from the queue
    W->>F: append event, buffered in memory
    Note over W,F: batch size reached or flush interval elapsed
    W->>F: flush, bulk write to disk

    App->>A: close at shutdown
    A->>A: enqueue poison marker behind all earlier events
    W->>F: append every remaining event
    W->>F: flush then close
    A-->>App: close returns after the worker has finished
